    <summary>
      (1) Derivation: CoreAncestorResolver.IntermediateRootColumns makes a child's stamp the root of WHATEVER it is filed under (communication / event / to-do / analysis: the four sprk_regarding{core}; invoice and budget: typed matter / project; document: the shared DocumentLinkFields root links; agreement and report card: sprk_regarding matter / project). Two different roots of one type = error. ClassifyStampSource is the one pair-based rule the cascade, the job and the resolver share.
      (2) Cascade: CoreAncestorRestamper.AfterWriteAsync is called after the write by PUT /api/v1/documents/{id}, associate-record, UpdateRecordActionCore (playbook node + ActionSeam), DataverseUpdateHandler and the field-mapping push; it writes only the stamp columns of the root types the source can carry, never a direct link or the owner; transitive (depth 4; cycles converge); a child failure is reported, the caller's write stands. The user-OBO AI update tool re-stamps INLINE through CoreAncestorAfterWriteRestamp (owner round 8 item 1, section 6.5 path B); until round 8 it enqueued the cascade (interpretation xvii, superseded).
      (3) Job: CoreAncestorStampReconciliationJob, ADR-036 IScheduledJob every 5 minutes (AddScheduledJob, unconditional): repairs stale copies and F-051-6 orphans; failed scan = failed run; claim per repair, completion marker scoped to the run; report-only switch CoreAncestor:StampReconciliation:WritesEnabled=false.
      (4) Enqueue: CoreAncestorRestampQueue + CoreAncestorRestampJobHandler (ADR-004, sdap-jobs, lazy Service Bus); since owner round 8 item 1 it carries the resolver's stale refusals only.
      (5) Resolver: 155's held branch replaced by the live comparison — equal resolves like a direct root; differ = 409 container_ancestor_stale + enqueue (transient for the inbound processor); unreadable 503; missing 409; transitive; filing loop 409; a secure securable source is a root; two roots of one type on a source = ambiguous. Office carrier: agree = direct link; differ + any secure = ambiguous; differ + none secure = direct link. Still held: service request; intermediates on rows that carry no copy; a pair alone naming an intermediate.
    </summary>
    <escalations>Neither trigger fired. Trigger 1: no path needs a transaction Dataverse lacks — in the window between an intermediate's write and its children's PATCHes the resolver refuses a stale copy (409), it never misfiles. Trigger 2: live max 2 stamped children under any one intermediate (cascade bounded at 5000 per table, depth 4; past it TRUNCATED and the job finishes). Owner round 8 (2026-10-03): xvii RESOLVED by item 1 (path B, see owner-round-8 below); xii is filed as work (156 item 13a). As flagged at the time: interpretation xvii — DataverseUpdateRecordHandler's own MUST rule forbids an app-only client, so its cascade is enqueued (seconds) rather than run in the same operation; and xii — the TypeScript stamp mirror still derives only the four columns (client-created children under invoice / document / agreement / budget / report card are unstamped until the job's next run).</escalations>
