        Item 1 (AC7, seed V1 survived the whole BFF unit suite): the branch is REACHABLE, so it stays, and a test now pins it. CreateTaskNodeExecutor passes the playbook's config.RegardingObjectType through as text. ActionSeam passes CreateTaskRequest.RegardingObjectType through, which CommunicationCreateTaskApplyService fills from a proposal's regardingObjectType. Neither checks the type against a list. RegardingFieldByEntity maps sprk_recordtype_ref to sprk_regardingrecordtype, and CoreAncestorResolver classes that type as Unclassified, which is a success, so the task is created. New test: ServerWriterAncestorStampingTests.CreateTask_WhenRegardingARecordTypeRow_KeepsItsTypedLookupAndWritesNoPair. In its world every type has a record-type row, sprk_recordtype_ref included, so a pair write would also replace the typed lookup. The test asserts that the task is created; that sprk_regardingrecordtype still names the filed record-type row (entity and id); that no sprk_regardingrecordid, sprk_regardingrecordurl or sprk_regardingrecordname is written; and that the record-type lookup is never called. Seed V1 (if (regardingField.Length &gt; 0)): 1 red.
